Add a fluentd path for JSON formatted OpenStack logs.

oslo.log can emit JSON instead of its text format, which keeps fields
such as the request context structured rather than packed into a
message string that a regular expression then has to pick apart again.
Until now, Kerbside and etcd have been the only services to use JSON
logging.

Add openstack_logging_json, defaulting to False. This is one switch
for every oslo.log service rather than a per service option, because
all of them share the single input in conf/input/00-global.conf.j2.
That input has one parser, so a mix of formats underneath it cannot be
read.

No service emits JSON yet, so this changes nothing until one is
converted. With the option off the rendered configuration is unchanged
apart from blank lines, which this template already produces from its
existing conditional.

Prompt: Michael asked how much work it would be to let every oslo.log
service in Kolla-Ansible log JSON using the parser added for Kerbside.

